   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.5. Increased capacity of constituents to develop fair and effective labour migration frameworks, institutions and services to protect migrant workers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Malaysian Trades Union Congress (MTUC) and civil society organizations Tenaganita, Persatuan Sahabat Wanita (PSWS) and Our Journey enhanced their MRC services (e.g. hotlines, counselling, legal aid, shelter, organizing, training, community outreach) to migrant workers, with  specific services for women migrant workers, as well as mainstreamed strategies that look into issues of gender, VAW, violence, harassment and trafficking). In 2020-2021  the organizations expanded their services to include delivery of humanitarian aid (food, PPE, hygiene products) to migrant workers affected by COVID-19. As a result, 76,017 (16,990 women) were able to access essential services and information that address issues of labour rights, safe migration, freedom of association, exploitation, abuse, violence, harassment and trafficking in persons. The ILO, with support from the European Union, Australia and United States provided financial resources and technical support through separate implementation agreements with the Malaysian Trades Union Congress and civil society organizations Tenaganita, Persatuan Sahabat Wanita Selangor, in order for them to operate Migrant Worker Resource Centers (MRCs), distribute COVID-19 emergency assistance, and provide services with particular focus on expanding access for women migrant workers. The ILO has also provided trainings to MRC staff on M&amp;E and financial reporting, as well as mainstreaming issues of gender, violence, harassment and trafficking into their service delivery strategies.

The ILO has also provided resources to the International Domestic Workers Federation (IDWF) to support the formation and operation of migrant domestic workers community networks in Malaysia, as well as to Our Journey to provide humanitarian assistance (including PPEs) to migrant workers affected by the COVID-19 pandemic.</narrative>
   </description>
